1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:09,312
Meet EVA, an Arch Linux desktop with its own Wayland
compositor. This is a beta: an evolving desktop, running

2
00:00:09,312 --> 00:00:11,485
here in one continuous take.

3
00:00:14,485 --> 00:00:23,513
Start with the launcher. Browse installed applications or
search for apps and local files. Choose a classic layout

4
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:25,968
or the circular Orbit launcher.

5
00:00:28,968 --> 00:00:37,435
Prisma is EVA's file manager. Open folders, preview
images, work with tabs and choose files from other

6
00:00:37,435 --> 00:00:41,170
applications, all through the same interface.

7
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:51,961
Super plus B opens the application shelf. See your running
apps together and switch between them, without filling the

8
00:00:51,961 --> 00:00:54,491
dock with duplicate application icons.

9
00:00:57,492 --> 00:01:05,185
Press Tab for the window overview. Move between virtual
desktops, select a window, and keep different tasks

10
00:01:05,185 --> 00:01:07,558
organized across your workspaces.

11
00:01:10,558 --> 00:01:18,673
Use Super plus Z to arrange windows. Snap offers several
layouts and checks application size limits before placing

12
00:01:18,673 --> 00:01:20,310
windows in their zones.

13
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:30,244
Super plus W opens the wallpaper picker. Choose a
background for each workspace and monitor, with animated

14
00:01:30,244 --> 00:01:32,598
transitions between your selections.

15
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:44,868
Settings brings the desktop together. Choose light or dark
appearance, adjust your accent color and explore window

16
00:01:44,868 --> 00:01:46,651
effects directly in EVA.

17
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:57,627
Make the bar your own. Drag modules into the beginning,
center or end. The layout keeps zones apart and stops

18
00:01:57,627 --> 00:01:59,822
additions when space runs out.

19
00:02:02,822 --> 00:02:09,782
Keyboard settings shows your configured layout and
editable shortcuts. Desktop and laptop defaults adapt to

20
00:02:09,782 --> 00:02:13,619
the hardware, while your custom combinations are
preserved.

21
00:02:17,049 --> 00:02:24,709
The system panel keeps CPU, memory, storage and available
hardware sensors in view. These readings come from the

22
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:27,103
machine running this demonstration.

23
00:02:30,103 --> 00:02:38,318
Play local media and control compatible players from the
desktop. The multimedia panel follows real playback, with

24
00:02:38,318 --> 00:02:41,272
artwork, progress and transport controls.

25
00:02:44,272 --> 00:02:53,976
Desktop companions add a playful corner to EVA. Care for a
pet, visit its habitat and use the local interactions

26
00:02:53,976 --> 00:02:55,882
without an AI account.

27
00:02:58,882 --> 00:03:05,693
The AI island connects to supported providers and
development agents. Online AI features require your own

28
00:03:05,693 --> 00:03:09,715
compatible service. No conversation is simulated in this
tour.

29
00:03:13,701 --> 00:03:22,320
EVA is available for x86 sixty-four PCs, with a graphical
installer and visual boot-theme settings. Download the

30
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:26,322
beta above and explore the desktop at your own pace.
